{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01040",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 3.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.84,
      "end_seconds": 8.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.94,
      "end_seconds": 22.64,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "Doctor, um, it's a low fever in the evenings. It's getting on my nerves now. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.28,
      "end_seconds": 29.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Alright, can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.24,
      "end_seconds": 37.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.76,
      "end_seconds": 41.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.02,
      "end_seconds": 70.85,
      "duration_seconds": 24.83,
      "text": "Well, for my pressure, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I'm on sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed for my migraines. Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever. I used to take ramipril, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.08,
      "end_seconds": 74.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.03,
      "end_seconds": 85.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Okay, so it's been ten days now. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.51,
      "end_seconds": 93.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "What do you do to make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.51,
      "end_seconds": 109.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "Paracetamol helps a bit. As for lump in my armpit, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.03,
      "end_seconds": 116.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Have you had a low fever in the evenings before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.58,
      "end_seconds": 124.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.21,
      "end_seconds": 130.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any cough, recent travel or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.72,
      "end_seconds": 146.34,
      "duration_seconds": 14.62,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, no cough, no recent travel, no diarrhoea. I did have itching all over at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.14,
      "end_seconds": 150.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, and what about chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.98,
      "end_seconds": 155.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.81,
      "end_seconds": 158.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.89,
      "end_seconds": 165.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.59,
      "end_seconds": 170.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.04,
      "end_seconds": 175.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.43,
      "end_seconds": 191.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.87,
      "end_seconds": 197.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.83,
      "end_seconds": 201.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.48,
      "end_seconds": 204.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.97,
      "end_seconds": 207.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.71,
      "end_seconds": 216.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "So, I've had high cholesterol, yes. High blood pressure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.99,
      "end_seconds": 218.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.18,
      "end_seconds": 226.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "I've got migraines. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.58,
      "end_seconds": 239.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Right, right. Right, so migraines is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 256.66,
      "end_seconds": 266.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 107 over 66, oxygen saturation is 95 percent, pulse 104, temperature 38.1."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.94,
      "end_seconds": 268.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.5,
      "end_seconds": 275.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.31,
      "end_seconds": 278.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.1,
      "end_seconds": 301.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "There's a firm, rubbery gland about two centimetres in the left armpit, not tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.28,
      "end_seconds": 305.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.38,
      "end_seconds": 322.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I can't feel your spleen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.52,
      "end_seconds": 325.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.88,
      "end_seconds": 357.47,
      "duration_seconds": 26.59,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards an enlarged gland with night sweats that needs a proper work-up. I can't rule out a blood condition yet. We shouldn't forget a lingering infection. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a low fever in the evenings for ten days, and no recent travel or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.52,
      "end_seconds": 361.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.07,
      "end_seconds": 374.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "I think an ultrasound of the armpit makes sense here, for lymph node. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 376.9,
      "end_seconds": 381.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "I can book that for Monday at 11:30 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.56,
      "end_seconds": 402.16,
      "duration_seconds": 19.6,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for night sweats. Keep a note of your temperature each evening. A chest X-ray is something we might do if this doesn't improve next month. I'd like to see you again in a week. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.61,
      "end_seconds": 405.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.65,
      "end_seconds": 408.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "So, all the best."
    }
  ]
}